      "content": "1. Genetics – Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Genetics is the study of heredity and variation in living organisms.",
        "Gregor Mendel established the fundamental principles of inheritance through his pea plant experiments.",
        "The three main Mendelian principles are the Law of Dominance, Law of Segregation, and Law of Independent Assortment.",
        "Genes located on chromosomes made of DNA serve as the structural and functional units of heredity.",
        "Patterns of inheritance are evaluated using Monohybrid (single trait) and Dihybrid (two traits) crosses."
      ],
      "id": "g9oyyra"
